Sure! To create an `InvokePolymorphicNode` for a range invocation, you’ll need to pass the instruction data (as a string) and set the `isRange` flag to `"true"` when calling the `InsnDecoder_invokePolymorphic` function.

Here’s a quick example of how you can do this:

```java
// Assume you have your instruction data as a string:
String instructionData = /* your instruction data here */;

// Call the function to create the InvokePolymorphicNode:
Object invokePolymorphicNode = functions.InsnDecoder_invokePolymorphic(
    new java.util.HashMap<String, Object>() {{
        put("insn", instructionData);
        put("isRange", "true");
    }}
);

// Now you can work with the created node:
System.out.println(invokePolymorphicNode);
```

